From ea169405532935720bcc4ae6c57500e5b3bd8e40 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ecogamezz <33791269+ecogamezz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 11:55:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] WowCraft: one interface at a time (C), overlay frames
 written in place, overlay flow report

- C switches the interfaces with the input: in Minecraft's mode WoW's interface is hidden, as
  Alt-Z hides it (UIParent), and Minecraft's HUD shows; in WoW's mode WoW's interface and cursor
  show and Minecraft's HUD hides, unless one of its screens is open. Typing in WoW's chat shows
  WoW's interface too; M, L, B and O switch to WoW's mode.
- Each overlay frame is written into the one texture in place, in the render world, instead of
  replacing the image asset's data every frame.
- Every 10 s while Minecraft is in its world the log says how many overlay frames Minecraft
  published and we took, and whether the newest one's pixels changed: a player reports Minecraft's
  HUD frozen on its first frame, which a stand-in Minecraft doesn't reproduce (its frames keep
  showing), so the next real run says which side stops.

Verified: cargo test --release -p benilla-app --no-default-features --lib wowcraft (44),
-p wowcraft-link (8); cargo build --release -p benilla --no-default-features; a live run with
mod/test/CutMinecraft: WoW's interface hidden in Minecraft's mode, the stand-in's moving hotbar
selection showing, ~96 frames published and taken per 10 s. The C switch itself was not pressed
live. Built on macOS (Intel) only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
